{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1580 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "591fdac237b79ee48fc7e67c2cf8a944fcb74a86fd2253ac46cdf0524ebacd55" :edb/db-before-t 1579 :edb/db-after-t 1580 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534892 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:31:41.390Z" 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186129531 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186129531 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." 13194139534892 17592186045417 false] [17592186281625 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/62/626cbf8e182d9eebb8b48026f07c5dd012c1096cc9568465f3648710ea0d07a4.png)\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(10y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}10{x}^{2}y+10{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5{x}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})+\\frac{5}{2}{(4-{x}^{2})}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{2}(4-{x}^{2})(2{x}^{2}+4-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}16-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{[16x-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(32-\\frac{32}{5}) \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186281625 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/62/626cbf8e182d9eebb8b48026f07c5dd012c1096cc9568465f3648710ea0d07a4.png)\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(10y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}10{x}^{2}y+10{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5{x}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})+\\frac{5}{2}{(4-{x}^{2})}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{2}(4-{x}^{2})(2{x}^{2}+4-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}16-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{[16x-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(32-\\frac{32}{5}) \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534892 17592186045417 false] [17592186281632 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186281632 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." 13194139534892 17592186045417 false] [17592186281633 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186281633 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139534892 17592186045417 false] [17592186281642 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that the region $D$ in polar coordinates can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,2\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nAlso, the mass density function in polar coordinates is \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({\\int }_{2}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{3}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-4)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186281642 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that the region $D$ in polar coordinates can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,2\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nAlso, the mass density function in polar coordinates is \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({\\int }_{2}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{3}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-4)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534892 17592186045417 false] [17592186442856 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442857 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442858 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442859 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442860 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442861 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1045 "Moments of Inertia of Laminas About the Coordinate Axes" 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1046 #edb/ref 17592186442860 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049331 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442856 1053 #uuid "eefcace8-eaae-544e-a20e-72207ae27112" 13194139534892 17592186045417 true] [17592186442857 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442861 13194139534892 175921860